course: dictionary
lesson: 991
title: One word, many meanings: body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word body is a good example. «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection» means the whole of a person, because the temperature of the whole body goes up.
explain: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head» uses body to mean the main part, not the head. The sentence sets the body against the head, so the clue is the contrast. Ask yourself: which meaning of body fits here?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Snailfish have soft bones and watery bodies» uses bodies, the plural of body, to mean the bodies of the fish. If your meaning makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Body is a noun. Its plural is bodies.
fact: Body can mean all of a person or an animal: head, arms, legs and everything inside.
fact: Body can mean the main part of a person or animal, not the head, arms or legs.
fact: Body can mean a dead person or animal, or the main part of something, like the body of a letter or a car.
fact: Body can also mean an object or a group, as in a body of water, a heavenly body or the student body.
exercise: «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection.» Which meaning of body fits here? | The main part of a car, not the wheels | *All of a person, with head, arms and legs | A group of students | A dead person
exercise: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head.» What does body mean here? | A small lump of rock | A group of lions | *The main part, not the head, arms or legs | A dead lion
exercise: Which word in «Snailfish have soft bones and watery bodies» is the plural of body? | watery | bones | *bodies | Snailfish
test: «Mia found the body of a small bird under the tree.» What does body mean here? | *A dead bird | A group of birds | A heavenly body in the sky | The wings of a bird
test: Which is the correct plural of body? | bodyes | body's | *bodies | bodys
exam: «The satanic leaf-tailed gecko has a body and tail that look like a dry curled leaf.» Which meaning of body fits? | A group of geckos | A heavenly body, like a planet | *All of the animal, with head, tail and legs | A dead gecko
